"""Level Factory 0.231.0 (the factory's roadmap 292): the enemy sights from the contract's body too.

The Laser Tag adapter wrote the contract's player body into every run's scenario and left the enemy's eye at Laser
Tag's 1.6. `agent_contract.read_player_body` reads the enemy's eye too: the contract's `characters.npc_standard` eye,
and the player's where that block states none, the contract's NPCs sharing the player's metrics until a distinct class
ships.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has been
worked out: `packages/validation/agent_contract.py` and `tests/unit/test_sight_follows_the_body.py` (anchored hunks);
`tests/unit/test_the_enemy_sights_from_the_contract.py` (new); VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from
a proven clone (`patches/lf_enemy_eye/gen_lf_enemy_eye.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a
second run refused (`patches/lf_enemy_eye/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_lf_enemy_eye.py
    cd level_factory && python -m pytest -q > out.txt 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"
"""
